Regional and Industry GDP Analytics: Statistical Testing, Forecasting, and Economic Segmentation
Overview

This project analyzes quarterly Gross Domestic Product (GDP) data across U.S. regions and industries to identify economic growth patterns, evaluate regional differences, forecast future GDP, and uncover economic similarities through statistical analysis and machine learning.

Using GDP by industry and region data from the United States, this project combines econometrics, statistical inference, machine learning, time-series forecasting, clustering, and interactive visualizations into a comprehensive economic analytics pipeline.

Objectives

This project aims to answer several key economic questions:

Which industries contribute the most to U.S. economic output?
Which regions exhibit the strongest economic growth?
Are regional growth differences statistically significant?
Which industries consistently outperform the national economy?
Can regions be grouped into distinct economic profiles?
Which industries move together over time?
Can future GDP be accurately forecast using statistical and machine learning models?
Which forecasting approach performs best?
Dataset

The dataset contains quarterly GDP values (in current dollars) for:

Multiple U.S. regions
Multiple industries
Quarterly observations over multiple years
Features
Variable	Description
GeoFIPS	Regional identifier
Region	U.S. Economic Region
IndustryID	BEA Industry Code
Industry	Industry Name
Quarterly GDP Columns	GDP values by quarter

The data is transformed into a long-format time-series structure for analysis.

